# Screenshot output from the e2e run. Nothing reads it: no spec compares against these, they are
# only ever written, and a full run rewrites all ~100 of them. Committed, that was 161MB of
# binaries churning on every run, which is most of what made .git a gigabyte. They still land on
# disk for looking at, the same as `screenshots/` above.
apps/client/e2e-out/
